**DEFINITION 8.1.** A retraction of a given domain $E$ is an approximable mapping $a : E \to E$ such that $a \circ a = a$. $\square$

The development is with the [retraction](1980_retraction.md) peer.

<!-- formalization -->

**Theorem (`definition_81`).** An approximable endomap is a retraction precisely when it equals its composite with itself.

*Proof.* By the definition of retraction. ∎
